      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|           DANCE AS POLITICAL INDICATOR                               |\n|                                                                      |\n|  POWER ASSERTS ITSELF      RESISTANCE USES DANCE                     |\n|  THROUGH DANCE             AGAINST POWER                             |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Louis XIV founds academy  Slave dances survive colonialism          |\n|  (centralizes culture)     (Congo Square, New Orleans)               |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Nazi Germany uses ballet  Capoeira disguises as dance               |\n|  as national prestige       (resists Portuguese suppression)         |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Soviet Union exports       Lindy Hop as Black cultural              |\n|  ballet (Cold War)          assertion (Harlem Renaissance)           |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Colonial India bans        Bharatanatyam revival as                 |\n|  devadasi dance             anti-colonial cultural identity          |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Flamenco made \"safe\"       Gitano communities maintain              |\n|  for tourism (regime)       the underground authentic form           |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
