      "text": "NATIVE AMERICAN GHOST DANCE (1889-1890):\n  Wovoka (Paiute prophet) -- vision of spiritual renewal\n  Ghost Dance: circular dance, reunite living and dead\n  Spread rapidly across Plains tribes (1889-1890)\n  U.S. government banned the dance (Circular 1372, 1883 Indian Religious\n  Crimes Code -- dance = \"heathenish practices\")\n  Sitting Bull arrested in connection with Ghost Dance activism\n  Massacre at Wounded Knee (Dec 29, 1890):\n    290 Lakota killed by 7th Cavalry\n    Immediately after Sitting Bull's arrest\n    In context of Ghost Dance suppression\n  The dance was the political act; the massacre was the response."
